A||||4||mrfixit58||Headlight question??||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||04-09-2000||12:28 PM||||Even after all the knowledge you've shed on this topic, I've got questions..<P>I volunteered to help fix a friend's non-functioning headlight in her 88 GT. She said that even when she turns the manual knob, the headlight doesn't want to go up. Have you heard of this before? Also, if I have to order parts, how do I make the headlights stay up with out the warning chime continuiously ringing?<P>I've heard that you can use motors from a Firebird. I've got a good motor from an 89 Firebird. Will this work?<P>Please help. I've never had to mess with these things and I want to make sure I get it right. Besides, she has promised the car to me when they move and it is CHERRY!<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodney||04-09-2000||12:52 PM||||87-88 headlight actuators are very durable and long lasting. Easy to rebuild. There are 3 shock absorbing dowels in each assembly. They in time grind into a powder. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/8788headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/8788headlight.htm</A> <P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||04-09-2000||12:54 PM||||Lets see if I can get it right this time??<BR> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/87-88headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/87-88headlight.htm</A> <P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||04-09-2000||08:21 PM||||Or I have them||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zman302||04-09-2000||10:01 PM||||I came across a site the other day that had a idea for the headlights that allows them to stay up and the chime doesnt chime.  splice in a switch to the white wire coming out of the headlight switch.  leave the switch in the off position and turn the lights on.  when you turn them out the doors will stay up untill you flip the switch to the on position.  I done this the other day and it works great.  should save alot of wear and tear on the motors and makes it nice to clean the headlights of dirt and grime.||||reg||1
